      "summary": ": Saturday/Rāhoroi Another cracker of a day is lined up at Treble Cone! The snow is skiing and riding beautifully right across the mountain, with fresh overnight grooming serving up lovely turns for those early morning laps. The Saddle is one big natural playground just waiting to be explored. Motatapu Chutes are Open! Weather: A mix of sun and cloud with the chance of a few light snow showers later in the day. Big Skite will be closed for race trainling until mid morning. Events on this weekend: Rise & Shine, Sunday 9th August, Ski touring race for a sunrise ascent, book on the website. Keep Kea Wild: Our cheeky local mountain parrot, kea, love to investigate, please don't leave food unattended. There are no landfill bins on the mountain, pack out what you bring in and help keep our kea wild and healthy. -- Home Basin Open Saddle Basin Open Matukituki Basin On-Hold Summit Slopes Open Motatapu Chutes Open Sundance Closed Backcountry Access Open Skinning Access Open Beginner Platter Open",
